{"duration": 48.63, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A Soviet engineer strapped a trembling dog into a cramped metal can.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.699}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Colleagues laughed, saying a stray could never survive a launch.", "start": 4.119, "end": 7.19}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Khrushchev demanded a \u201cspace spectacular\u201d for the October Revolution anniversary.", "start": 7.61, "end": 12.054}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Korolev had less than four weeks to finish a new satellite.", "start": 12.274, "end": 15.093}, {"beat": 2, "text": "He grabbed a small dog cage and bolted it onto the rocket.", "start": 15.313, "end": 18.383}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like testing a car\u2019s seatbelt on a dummy before letting a driver sit behind the wheel.", "start": 18.803, "end": 23.771}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The real reason: Laika was a living test for the cabin\u2019s air system.", "start": 24.191, "end": 27.898}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The capsule held an oxygen maker, a filter to soak up bad air, and a fan that turned on when it got too hot.", "start": 28.118, "end": 34.104}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Scientists watched her breathing, pulse, and temperature from the ground.", "start": 34.324, "end": 37.86}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The twist? The mission never planned to bring her home.", "start": 38.28, "end": 40.743}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Laika was a one\u2011way sacrifice, proving the cabin could keep any creature alive, even if that creature never left orbit.", "start": 40.963, "end": 47.51}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.145, "end": 0.195, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Soviet", "start": 0.27, "end": 0.62, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "engineer", "start": 0.645, "end": 1.295, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "strapped", "start": 1.395, "end": 1.695, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "a", "start": 1.72, "end": 1.745, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "trembling", "start": 1.795, "end": 2.17, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "dog", "start": 2.22